        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "tables": [],
  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Discussion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "To delete an Xcode Cloud product, call this endpoint using the HTTP `DELETE` method like this:",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "```swift\nhttps://api.appstoreconnect.apple.com/v1/ciProducts/9ad354b0-f380-40d3-b94f-dd5225b8b3d5\n```",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "App Store Connect confirms the deletion by responding with the `HTTP/1.1 204 No Content` HTTP status code.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Important**\n>\n>  Deleting an Xcode Cloud product permanently deletes all workflows, including their build history and artifacts. Only delete an Xcode Cloud product when you’re confident that you don’t need its workflows, build history, or artifacts anymore. Instead of deleting a product, deactivate its workflows to preserve the product and its build history and artifacts. For more information about deactivating a workflow, see `Developing-a-Workflow-Strategy-for-Xcode-Cloud`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Xcode/Developing-a-Workflow-Strategy-for-Xcode-Cloud"
          ]
        }
